    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d484">

                <pb facs="0456" n="340" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg340"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 738.3915/92.]</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to Haiti to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-01-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 8, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I am assured by the President of Haiti that on December 23, 1911, he ordered the
                    frontier authorities to prevent Dominican revolutionists from entering Haitian
                        territory.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d484-f1"/> The Haitian authorities, says the
                    President, are greatly hampered by lack of support by the Dominican authorities
                    on the frontier; prior to the death of President Cáceres<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d484-f2"/> they acted in conjunction with the Haitian authorities,
                    but since then they have been inactive.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Furniss</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
